  "x-metriplane-semantic-checks": [
    "UNRESOLVED requires null binding and blocks live consumption; every binding reference must resolve to the exact backend live_binding C digest.",
    "Bound adapter_id must name a separately implemented/reviewed existing-owner adapter; a string cannot dynamically select executable code or establish supported service semantics.",
    "All original sidecars are enumerated, safe regular files and raw-hash bound under the supplied bundle before effects. Configuration contains references to credentials, never secret values.",
    "Owner approval must be independently expected and authentic; neither adjacent files, two independence_group strings nor two same-host directories establish independent durable stores.",
    "Payload A/B actual administration, resource identity, retention, failure and revocation domains must satisfy the original owner-approved independence policy with original proof.",
    "Preflight outputs bind immutable raw registry bytes; no preflight/receipt digest is written back into that registry, avoiding registry/preflight cycles.",
    "attempt-index also fences promotion-lock operations under the existing owner; success-chain/LKG namespaces remain distinct. No separate unbound lock or second release state machine.",
    "Main-health backend labels refer only to existing governed main-health owners and protected state. A binding cannot redirect or independently mutate protected main-health branches.",
    "Isolated preflight/test and production namespaces cannot alias; preflight never mutates production heads. Complete per-capability operation/readback evidence remains mandatory."
  ]
